(For covered services first operating on or after 1 January 2026, those duties apply immediately on first) Tj T*
(operation.) Tj T*
(Article 5. Incorporated duties) Tj T*
(When an operator delegates export fulfillment to an external fulfillment provider, that provider must) Tj T*
(implement the portable-copy software function and perform the same delivery duty required by Article) Tj T*
(2\(1\), with the same seven-day period and the definitions in Article 1. Delegation does not remove the) Tj T*
(operator's own duty.) Tj T*
(Article 6. Context and separate configuration duties) Tj T*
(1. Repository storage means the storage surface used by the covered service for customer-created records.) Tj T*
(An audit entry means the event record about an export request. This paragraph supplies context and) Tj T*
(definitions; it creates no independent duty, prohibition or permission.) Tj T*
(2. The operator must maintain a software configuration identifying the relevant covered service. For its) Tj T*
(export function, the operator must record the authorization decision in an audit entry and must record) Tj T*
(completion or failure with its timestamp in the audit entry. These two audit duties are compatible and) Tj T*
(both must survive a combined representation. The operator must implement appropriate software safeguards) Tj T*
(protecting customer-created records during processing and export. A repository assessment may inspect) Tj T*
(storage encryption as one narrower evidence slice; this does not replace the safeguards duty or require a) Tj T*
(particular cipher.) Tj T*
(Article 7. Delegated fulfillment and direction) Tj T*
(Actor A is the covered-service operator and holder of Article 2\(1\). Actor B is the fulfillment provider.) Tj T*
(If A delegates export fulfillment to B, A must maintain a software configuration identifying B as its) Tj T*
(delegate for that service, and B must implement the delegated portable-copy software path on behalf of A.) Tj T*
(B performs fulfillment while A remains responsible for Article 2\(1\). B's express duty in Article 5 does) Tj T*
(not transfer or replace A's duty. B delegating to A is not this condition. The customer is the requesting) Tj T*
(record owner and beneficiary; an auditor owes no export-fulfillment duty.) Tj T*
(Article 8. Conditional permission and evidence) Tj T*
(The operator may restrict access to the export interface only while a documented, specific security) Tj T*
(incident makes access unsafe. The restriction must end when that condition ceases. Evidence must) Tj T*
(demonstrate whether that condition holds and whether any restriction respects it. This Article does not) Tj T*
(require automatic blocking, automatic unblocking, or any other particular technical implementation.) Tj T*
ET
